BOINC docker_wrapper: memory use of the container from /proc.

The wrapper reports the container's working set to the client (wss in
boinc_report_app_status_aux), taken from MemUsage of "stats --no-stream". With rootless
Podman under the client service the container has no cgroup of its own (see 0002), and
MemUsage is the memory of the enclosing cgroup: all BOINC tasks plus page cache, e.g.
4.8 GB for a gnina task that uses far less. The client sums these values against its RAM
limit and estimates new tasks of the app version from them, so on a 64 GB host further
tasks went to "waiting for memory" after about 6 running tasks with RAM mostly free.
On Linux the WSS is now the sum of the resident set sizes of the container's process
tree (field rss of /proc/PID/stat, same tree as the CPU time); the stats value is only
used if the tree can't be read. The log line at the end of the container also shows the
peak memory use, to help set rsc_memory_bound.
Written for server_release/1.6/1.6.2 on top of 0002 and 0004 to 0009.

